1
00:05:48,750 --> 00:05:54,750
A new spin on the old song and dance.

2
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:43,500
Love's Labour's Lost is a comedy, music, romance
film directed by Kenneth Branagh.

3
00:17:26,250 --> 00:17:32,250
A scholarly king and his three companions swear off the society of women for three years, only to have a
diplomatic visit from a French princess and her three ladies-in-waiting thwart their intentions.

4
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:21,000
The King (Ferdinand), played by Alessandro Nivola.

5
00:29:03,750 --> 00:29:09,750
The Princess, played by Alicia Silverstone.

6
00:34:52,500 --> 00:34:58,500
Rosaline, played by Natascha McElhone.

7
00:40:41,250 --> 00:40:47,250
Berowne, played by Kenneth Branagh.

8
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Maria, played by Carmen Ejogo.

9
00:52:18,750 --> 00:52:24,750
Longaville, played by Matthew Lillard.

10
00:58:07,500 --> 00:58:13,500
Love's Labour's Lost is a 2000 British musical romantic comedy film written, directed by and
starring Kenneth Branagh, based on the comic play of the same name by William Shakespeare.

11
01:03:56,250 --> 01:04:02,250
The first feature film to be made of this lesser-known comedy, Branagh's fourth film
of a Shakespeare play was a box-office and critical disappointment.

12
01:09:45,000 --> 01:09:51,000
The cast includes Shakespearean veterans such as Timothy Spall, Richard Briers and Geraldine McEwan, alongside Hollywood
actors Alicia Silverstone and Matthew Lillard and Broadway and West End stars such as Nathan Lane and Jimmy Yuill.

13
01:15:33,750 --> 01:15:39,750
As a result of its poor commercial performance, Miramax shelved its three-picture deal with
Branagh, who subsequently returned to Shakespeare with As You Like It in 2006.

14
01:21:22,500 --> 01:21:28,500
The film explores themes of dance, musical, romance.

15
01:27:11,250 --> 01:27:17,250
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
